  "title": "Gateway to the Bieszczady",
  "lead": "An open-air museum of wooden architecture and an Icon Museum. A perfect base for Bieszczady trips.",
  "body": "<h2>Skansen and Icons</h2><p>Sanok is a town that combines the function of a gateway to the Bieszczady with that of an important cultural center. Here is one of the largest Folk Architecture Museums in Europe — an open-air museum where you can see what villages and small towns in these lands looked like a hundred years ago.</p><p>The Historical Museum in Sanok has one of the largest collections of icons in Poland — over 2,000 exhibits showing the richness of Carpathian church art. It is worth devoting at least two hours to it to truly appreciate their beauty.</p><h2>Market Square and Surroundings</h2><p>The market square in Sanok is a quiet place where you can sit in a café and watch the life of the town. It is worth paying attention to the historic townhouses and the Church of the Transfiguration, which is one of the oldest monuments of the town.</p><p>A walk along the San is, in turn, a perfect way to end the day. The river, bridges, hills in the background — all this forms a landscape that is a foretaste of what awaits tourists in the Bieszczady themselves.</p>",
  "tip": "Visit the Sanok Skansen with a guide or audio guide. Without ethnographic context, most exhibits will remain incomprehensible.",
